  "behavior": [
    "An explicit existing-store operation checks original root and exact retained state, authenticates policy and independent recovery-key possession proof, and atomically preserves signed policy/floor while installing v2 metadata.",
    "Original open/provision paths still refuse implicit enrollment or overwrites. A live lease is Busy; missing/corrupt storage never becomes first use.",
    "Exact enrolled configuration is idempotent. The original retry rejects changed policy/root or conflicting trust/proof. It is a configuration predicate, not a fresh-commit receipt.",
    "Real precommit/postcommit process cuts, postcommit unwind/result loss, and injected real-backend sync failure retain the original floor. Swift cancellation closes undelivered ownership after actual commit.",
    "Both enabled/disabled u32::MAX policies can be enrolled without rollback, then independently recover the online authority. Enrollment cannot reset existing recovery history."
  ],
  "retained_failures": {
    "ffi-01": "New test expected Policy for stale input; existing ABI correctly maps StoreError::Stale to Closed. Corrected exact assertion, retained production mapping; other failures cascaded from poisoned test serialization guard.",
